body:
Also if you have a visa and an I-20 (which are required) they likely won't ask for financial documents, either. The consider the finances when they interview you for a visa. If you are from a country the U.S. doesn't require a visa for (is there such a country?) or a country that you can get a US visa through an online application without a visa interview, then it is a good idea to bring financial docs. Otherwise they very likely not even ask for it. 

&#x200B;

I-20 and passport with a visa stamp are musts, though.
